## graphify (vendored in full)

- Location in this repo: `.claude/skills/graphify/` (version 0.9.16)
- Upstream: https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify
- Author: Safi Shamsi
- License: MIT (SPDX: MIT)
- Local modifications (not in upstream):
  - `SKILL.md` Step 1, and the extras tips in `SKILL.md` and
    `references/add-watch.md`, install `graphifyy` only at the version in
    `.claude/skills/graphify/.graphify_version`, with no `--upgrade` and no
    `--break-system-packages` fallback. Setup stops and asks the owner when the
    pin is missing or the pinned install fails (skill-safety-59f9427a).
  - Semantic extraction dispatches read-only subagents that return their JSON
    as text for the parent to write, instead of general-purpose subagents
    holding Write and Bash, and `/graphify add` asks the owner to confirm each
    URL before fetching it (skill-safety-5f9c118a). Ceiling: where the
    harness's read-only subagent type still carries a shell, the instruction
    not to run shell commands is prompt-level only.
  - `SKILL.md` semantic extraction uses Gemini only when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is set
    and the owner confirms uploading this corpus; `GOOGLE_API_KEY` no longer
    selects it, and without a yes the subagent path runs
    (skill-safety-39614de9). Ceiling: this governs what the skill tells the
    agent to run; a graphify CLI flow given `--backend gemini` by hand is
    outside it.
  - `references/query.md`'s three `save-result` steps (query, path, explain)
    pass the answer through a quoted heredoc into a temporary file read with
    `--answer-file`, and single-quote the question, node labels and any
    `--correction`, instead of substituting the answer into a double-quoted
    shell argument where backticks and `$(...)` execute (skill-safety-eabeab65).
- Generated content: the `## graphify` section formerly in CLAUDE.md was
  generated by `graphify claude install` (graphify 0.9.16); its four rules now
  live, locally modified only by relocation, in `.claude/rules/graphify.md`.

